) values (
  'QUESTION', 'question:sq-a3-05', 'Advanced · Stage 3, Consent and End-of-Life Ethics, In Depth · Stage Quiz', 'What is the legal position of a living will in South Africa?',
  'MEDICAL', 2, 'APPROVED',
  'No statute gives a living will binding force (checked 2026-09-24): SA Law Commission, ''Euthanasia and the Artificial Preservation of Life'', Project 86 report (November 1998) - draft ''End of Life Decisions Act 1999'' never enacted; National Health Amendment Bill [B8-2019] (living wills and durable power of attorney), introduced 27 February 2019, lapsed 7 May 2019 (pmg.org.za/bill/875); the Act''s s 7(1)(a)(i) recognises only a written mandate. Clarke v Hurst NO 1992 (4) SA 630 (D), as described in the Project 86 report paras 5.127-5.132: withdrawal of artificial feeding not unlawful by the boni mores; the order was not founded on the living will', 'Keyed answer and explanation checked against: No statute gives a living will binding force (checked 2026-09-24): SA Law Commission, ''Euthanasia and the Artificial Preservation of Life'', Project 86 report (November 1998) - draft ''End of Life Decisions Act 1999'' never enacted; National Health Amendment Bill [B8-2019] (living wills and durable power of attorney), introduced 27 February 2019, lapsed 7 May 2019 (pmg.org.za/bill/875); the Act''s s 7(1)(a)(i) recognises only a written mandate. Clarke v Hurst NO 1992 (4) SA 630 (D), as described in the Project 86 report paras 5.127-5.132: withdrawal of artificial feeding not unlawful by the boni mores; the order was not founded on the living will'
) on conflict (entity_type, entity_ref, claim) do update set
